 say that word on  television you asked me to be on here it  must be a dream of any comedian to get  to share a room with both Steve Martin  and Martin Short but that dream quickly  turned into a bit of a nightmare when  the two legends sat down on Jimmy  Fallon's couch and immediately said  about roasting him hard you proved the  tall handsome white men can make it in  show business  while they do it very playfully there  are some real jabs in there Martin Short  goes so far as to tell Fallon that no  late night host pretends to care the way  he does the two comedy heroes barely let  Jimmy get a question in and instead just  do 10 minutes of improv making fun of  each other and Jimmy himself they crack  jokes about how on  funny his monologue is make a ton of  political jokes and make up stories  about just about anything except for the  show that they came on to plug it might  not be the most productive interview or  even an interview at all but it's no  less entertaining Canadian heartthrob  Shawn Mendes has graced the Jimmy Fallon  show not once but twice and both have  been pretty awkward the first time in  2016 saw Shawn sitting in with the band  for Jimmy's bit called hashtag fall  songs in which Mendes sang tweets about  fall to the tune of famous songs the  first one went okay but when Jimmy gave  him the wrong cue for the second song  Mendes wasn't afraid to call him out  about it he then made a joke about Jimmy  being old instead of playing along  Fallon seemed to get confused by the  remark and left Mendes hanging in the  awkwardness trying to cover up his first  quip by claiming that Jimmy isn't old  Shawn is just very young which you know  is true the whole thing got off to a  very strange start but the young pop  star quickly recovered by nailing all of  the other songs  Joaquin Phoenix has never been the  easiest guy to interview just ask David  Letterman what well can you tell us  about your days with the Unabomber the  notoriously shy actor only does press  when he absolutely has to and is clearly  very uncomfortable about it so when he  came on Jimmy Fallon's show to promote  Joker things got awkward just as you  might expect them to Fallon starts  trying to play a game with Joaquin in  which he has a bunch of facts on a card  that may or may not be true and the  point is for the audience to guess which  is true and which is not we think but  the thing is he never explains exactly  what Joaquin is supposed to do and they  spend most of their time just trying to  clarify what the rules are  we'll give this one to Jimmy Fallon it  must be really hard to talk to Ricky  Gervais not only is he incredibly quick  he's intensely opinionated and will  barrel right through any conversation  without letting you get a word in  edgewise  as soon as Gervais sits down on Fallon  Jimmy tells him that he looks great  Gervais jumps right in to shut that  compliment down accusing the host of  being sarcastic  before monologuing for the next four and  a half minutes straight I look great  yeah is that sarcasm no Jimmy has no  choice but to just watch and laugh  forgoing any chance at getting a  question in and instead of giving in  Fallon keeps looking to his producers  and down at his desk shaking his head in  disbelief at one point he even crumples  up his notes indicating that there's no  point in even trying but it all gets a  little too real when Gervase lays into  obese children and then drops an f-bomb  Fallon stops laughing altogether and  looks off-camera clearly being told to  wrap it up fast a beast was the polite  word that was the polite word so we  didn't have to say [ __ ] the most  infamous Jimmy Fallon misstep has got to  be his interview with Donald Trump while  he was still only in the running for  president of the United States Jimmy  Fallon took it upon himself to invite  The Apprentice star on his show and it  went well not great early on when Jimmy  jokingly asks Trump if he still wants to  do this an audience member can be heard  shouting don't do it before Trump can  answer you you still have time do you  still want to do this I think this time  I then came the moment that caused a  huge media storm in a move that he has  since gone on to regret Jimmy playfully  ruffled Trump's hair at the very end of  the interview as the audience went wild  so did the media and the moment would go  down in history who some of those were  just painful what did you think of this  video what was your favorite  cringe-worthy moment is there a good one  that we missed let us know down in the  comments and don't forget to hit that  subscribe button to keep up with all of  the latest videos from the things  [Music]
 

